diff --git a/docs/design/streaming_weight_loading.md b/docs/design/streaming_weight_loading.md
index 8fb55df61b94ad2064483d3d24810fddff95987e..1d85ccfe1731876dd0dae39f626052387777d598 100644
--- a/docs/design/streaming_weight_loading.md
+++ b/docs/design/streaming_weight_loading.md
@@ -1,5 +1,9 @@
 # Proposal: bounded streaming weight loading
 
+In this tree the `b12x` load format and its adapter are gone: `--load-format
+direct` (`vllm/model_executor/model_loader/direct_loader.py`) is the bounce-ring
+path below, ported into vLLM. The rest of this proposal is kept as written.
+
 Status: the C99 O_DIRECT transport and b12x vLLM adapter load ordinary
 PyTorch CUDA tensors. The loader owns bounded I/O buffers and retains destination
 references until completion. Models use their normal allocation paths.
diff --git a/docs/features/tool_calling.md b/docs/features/tool_calling.md
index 2e8178d392adb72311025f1f917dc57b7ea34b2e..5d7b0a90688251e2ff88eeffd843e2815230275d 100644
--- a/docs/features/tool_calling.md
+++ b/docs/features/tool_calling.md
@@ -380,6 +380,12 @@ DeepSeek-specific role, not a standard OpenAI message role. Other unknown roles
 remain invalid. The encoding contract follows the
 [DeepSeek V4.1 reference](https://huggingface.co/deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash/blob/dba1be0a40aa45a94ad051997016db3960a90277/encoding/README.md).
 
+With `--tool-call-parser deepseek_v41`, output token IDs distinguish genuine DSML markers from copies spelled with ordinary tokens, including inside string arguments. This guard also works without a reasoning parser. Without token IDs, DSML matching remains text-based. In token-ID mode, text between and after tool-call blocks is returned as content.
+
+When auto tool choice is enabled and both `--tool-call-parser deepseek_v41` and `--reasoning-parser deepseek_v41` are selected, one engine parses reasoning and tools together, preserving token provenance across the transition. Text-spelled markers remain text in reasoning too. Requests without tools, or with `tool_choice="none"`, preserve DSML call markup as content instead of dropping it, with or without token IDs. Prompt reasoning-state detection stops at assistant, user and system role boundaries: a prompt that already closes reasoning starts in content, while a closing marker from an earlier turn does not disable reasoning.
+
+Under strict required and named tool choices, token-origin provenance remains enforced inside `<think>...</think>` while post-`</think>` constrained DSML output accepts markers spelled with ordinary tokens so string-based structural tags always extract as tool calls.
+
 ### OpenAI OSS Models (`openai`)
 
